#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:417
msgid "Connectors"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:482
msgid "Tune individual OpenStation behaviors. Each toggle affects only your account and takes effect immediately — no reload required. Watch the dot in the OpenStation Preferences title bar to see when a change has been saved."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:490
msgid "AI assistant"
msgstr ""

#. %s: keyboard shortcut, e.g. ⌘K or Ctrl+K
#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:498
msgid "Adds an AI mode to the %s site assistant. Ask in plain language to find content, get around wp-admin, and answer questions about your site. Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:507
#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:545
msgid "This feature requires an AI provider configured in"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:518
#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:552
msgid "Settings → Connectors"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:532
msgid "Score new comments with AI"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:538
msgid "Scores every new comment for spam and hostility, folding the result into the spam confidence shown in the Comments window. Site-wide, off by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:567
msgid "Draws arrowed connector lines between windows showing related content — a post and its comments or media, or two posts that link to each other. The line style and when the lines show live in Effects → Window links. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:573
msgid "Bring related windows to front"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:579
msgid "Clicking a window surfaces the windows directly tied to it — a parent brings up all of its children, a child brings up its parent — rising to just below the one you clicked, without stealing focus."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:586
msgid "Highlight related windows"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:592
msgid "While a group member is focused, its related windows get an accent outline and a soft glow so the family is recognizable at a glance."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:600
msgid "Show desktop when clicking the wallpaper"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:607
msgid "macOS-style gesture: a left click on the empty desktop minimizes every window, and a second click restores them. When on, the matching \"Show desktop\" entry is removed from the wallpaper context menu — the click gesture replaces it. Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:614
msgid "Show post/page status ribbon"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:621
msgid "Paints a diagonal corner ribbon — Draft, Pending, Private, or Scheduled — on WP Explorer tiles whose post status isn’t published. Off hides every ribbon; tiles still respect their dimmed-icon treatment so unpublished items remain visible at a glance. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:628
msgid "Enable developer mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:633
msgid "Unlocks developer-facing surfaces meant for plugin authors: the Starter Widget appears in the add-widget picker, and the OpenStation Preferences → Components tab runs its intentional missing-import-warner demo (a console banner plus three deliberate console.error entries). Off by default so regular users don’t see developer noise."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:640
msgid "Folder sharing"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:645
msgid "Lets you share desktop folders with other users or roles, with read or read+write access. When off, every share-related affordance (Share button, invites, \"Leave shared folder\") disappears from your shell and the heartbeat stops delivering share payloads to your session. Other users are unaffected. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:658
msgid "Deleting…"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:659
msgid "Delete folder sharing data"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:662
msgid "Site-wide destructive action (admin only). Drops every shares table — invites, decisions, share rows. Empty tables are recreated immediately so the feature still works for anyone who wants to start fresh. Use this on sites that never needed sharing to clear the data outright."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:672
msgid "WordPress Heartbeat rate"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:679
msgid "Fast — 15s (not recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:680
msgid "Medium — 30s"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:681
msgid "Slow — 45s"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:682
msgid "Very slow — 60s (default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:686
msgid "How often the WordPress Heartbeat API runs. Faster = quicker live updates (autosaves, lock checks, the heartbeat widget) at the cost of more server traffic. 15 s triples server load vs. the 60 s default — use sparingly. 30 s and 45 s require a page reload to apply exactly; 15 s and 60 s take effect immediately."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:698
msgid "Resetting…"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:699
msgid "Reset what’s-new dialogs"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:702
msgid "Re-shows the one-time introduction dialog the next time you open each redesigned native window."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:709
msgid "Beta features"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:710
msgid "Experimental redesigns of core admin screens. Off by default — opt in to try them. Each toggle affects only your account and takes effect immediately, no reload required."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:716
msgid "Use the native Posts window"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:721
msgid "Beta — off by default. Turn on to replace the classic Posts list iframe with a native, table-driven window: sticky header, server-paginated rows, multi-select bulk actions, and a sub-row preview. Toggle off any time to return to the classic screen."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:728
msgid "Use the native Pages window"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:733
msgid "Beta — off by default. Turn on for the same table-driven experience as the Posts window, tailored for Pages: a Parent column, hierarchical sort, and a lock indicator when another user is editing a page. Toggle off any time to return to the classic screen."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:740
msgid "Use the native Users window"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:745
msgid "Beta — off by default. Turn on for a native Users list with bulk role change, last-login tracking, live online indicators, click-to-copy email, and one-click password resets. Capability-gated — readers see a read-only view, role assignment respects WordPress role permissions."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:752
msgid "Use the native Plugins window"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:757
msgid "Beta — off by default. Turn on for a native two-tab Plugins window: an Installed list with bulk activate / deactivate / delete, and a Browse gallery powered by the WordPress.org repository — rich detail flyout with screenshots, ratings histogram, and recent reviews. Drag a .zip onto the window to install, or drag a card from Browse to the dock to pin it."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:764
msgid "Use the native Comments window"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings/sections/features.ts:769
msgid "Beta — off by default. Turn on for a native two-pane Comments window: a rail of conversations filtered by Pending / All / Spam / Trash / Mine, and the selected thread’s full nested reply chain beside it. Every message carries Reply, Edit, Approve, Spam and Trash inline, with a docked composer that repoints to whichever message you answer. Opening “Comments” on a post scopes the window to that post."
msgstr ""

